-- title:
--   Traces commute with residues under a regular prolongation
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, let $F$ be a field with an $L$-algebra structure, and let $\bar F$ be a field with a $k$-algebra structure. Let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with residue field $\bar F$, that is: a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ together with a ring homomorphism $R.\mathrm{residue} : R.\mathrm{integers} \to \bar F$ such that an element of $L$ lies in $A$ exactly when its image in $F$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the residue map is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$, it is compatible with $A \to k \to \bar F$, and every nonzero $f \in F$ admits $c \in L$ with $c \cdot f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ of nonzero residue. Let $x \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ have residue $\bar x$ transcendental over $k$, assume $\operatorname{finrank}_{k(\bar x)} \bar F > 0$ (so $\bar F/k(\bar x)$ is finite), and assume $\operatorname{finrank}_{L(x)} F = \operatorname{finrank}_{k(\bar x)} \bar F$, where $L(x)$ and $k(\bar x)$ denote the intermediate fields generated by $x$ and by $\bar x$. Then for every $z \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ the element $\operatorname{Tr}_{F/L(x)}(z)$, viewed in $F$, lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and its residue equals the image in $\bar F$ of $\operatorname{Tr}_{\bar F/k(\bar x)}(R.\mathrm{residue}\, z)$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of traces with Deuring's constant reduction of a function field: under the degree-preserving hypothesis, reduction at the prolongation $R$ carries $\operatorname{Tr}_{F/L(x)}$ to $\operatorname{Tr}_{\bar F/k(\bar x)}$ on integral elements. It is used in the construction of bases adapted to a family of prolongations, and in the reduction of regular differentials and $q$-expansions on modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_RegularProlongation_exists_residue_trace_eq_trace_residue_of_finrank_eq.lean

import Mathlib
